"""
Where the beaker touches the finger pads: MEASUREMENT ONLY (David, Oct 26, step 4; hypothesis: the fingers hold the beaker by their tips). Normal layout, beaker total 0.20 kg, one episode.

    MUJOCO_GL=egl python experiments/grip_pad_contact.py --out data/grip_pad/<name>

At three moments (the end of the closing, the end of the lift at the handoff, the end of the place's DOWN) and, for the extents, over every tick from the closing to the end of the carry:
  a  per finger: the pad's own size (the finger's collision mesh patch within 1 mm of its inner face, as src/gripper_geometry finds the pad centre), the contact points of the beaker on it in the pad's
     coordinates (along the approach axis from the pad's tip and from the patch centre, across the pad's width), and the extent and number of the contact points (the patch);
  b  the beaker's axis against the pad centre: the perpendicular distance, along the approach axis, along the closing axis, and the fingertips' position against the axis;
  d  on a copy of the state at the end of the closing: the beaker moved toward the palm (the hand going deeper) by 0 to 30 mm along the approach axis, the smallest distance of the beaker's geoms to
     the palm / hand body and to the other hand and arm parts;
  e  the grasp height against the beaker's centre of mass.
The friction and geometry of the model are read from the compiled model (c).
"""

import argparse
import gc
import json
import os
import sys
from pathlib import Path

PROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))
sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT / "experiments"))
